IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa15-nouns`

-- coa15-ch7.l4: Part 18, Chapter 7 (Supplementary provisions), ss 733 to 737 (lines 9617-9668 of ukpga-2006-46.txt).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat. Section 737 (the Secretary of State's power to modify this Part by regulations) is machinery and
-- has no function here. Reading a result: as in coa15-ch1.l4.

DECLARE `s 733(1) act in Chapter 7` IS ONE OF
    `s 733(1) transfer an amount to the capital redemption reserve`

DECLARE `s 735(6) other claim` IS ONE OF
    `s 735(6)(a) a debt or liability of the company other than one due to members in their character as such`
    `s 735(6)(b) an amount due in satisfaction of rights as to capital or income preferred to the rights as to capital attaching to the shares`
    `s 735(6) an amount due to members in satisfaction of their rights as members, other than preferred rights`
    `s 735(6) a claim of another kind`

-- ---- s 733: the capital redemption reserve ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9619 | (1) In the following circumstances a company must transfer amounts to a reserve, called the “capital redemption reserve”.
@ref s 733(1) In the following circumstances a company must transfer amounts to a reserve, called the capital redemption reserve (src:9619-9619)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 733(1) act in Chapter 7`
`s 733(1) the company must transfer the amount to the capital redemption reserve` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 733(1) transfer an amount to the capital redemption reserve`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 733: an amount was not transferred to the capital redemption reserve"

-- src:9620 | (2) Where under this Part shares of a limited company are redeemed or purchased wholly out of the company's profits, the amount by which the company's issued share capital is diminished in accordance with—
-- src:9621 | (a) section 688(b) (on the cancellation of shares redeemed), or
-- src:9622 | (b) section 706(b)(ii) (on the cancellation of shares purchased),
-- src:9623 | must be transferred to the capital redemption reserve.
@ref s 733(2) Where shares are redeemed or purchased wholly out of the company's profits, the amount by which the issued share capital is diminished must be transferred to the capital redemption reserve (src:9620-9623)
GIVEN `shares of a limited company are redeemed or purchased under Part 18 wholly out of the company's profits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount by which the issued share capital is diminished in accordance with section 688(b) or section 706(b)(ii)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 733(2) the amount to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` MEANS
    IF `shares of a limited company are redeemed or purchased under Part 18 wholly out of the company's profits`
    THEN `the amount by which the issued share capital is diminished in accordance with section 688(b) or section 706(b)(ii)`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where under this Part shares of a limited company are redeemed or purchased wholly out of the company's profits"

-- src:9624 | (3) If—
-- src:9625 | (a) the shares are redeemed or purchased wholly or partly out of the proceeds of a fresh issue, and
-- src:9626 | (b) the aggregate amount of the proceeds is less than the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased,
-- src:9627 | the amount of the difference must be transferred to the capital redemption reserve.
-- src:9628 | This does not apply in the case of a private company if, in addition to the proceeds of the fresh issue, the company applies a payment out of capital under Chapter 5 or under section 692(1ZA) in making the redemption or purchase.
@ref s 733(3) If shares are redeemed or purchased out of the proceeds of a fresh issue that are less than their nominal value, the difference must be transferred, unless a private company also applies a payment out of capital (src:9624-9628)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed or purchased wholly or partly out of the proceeds of a fresh issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aggregate amount of the proceeds` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased` IS A NUMBER
      `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in addition to the proceeds of the fresh issue the company applies a payment out of capital under Chapter 5 or under section 692(1ZA) in making the redemption or purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 733(3) the amount of the difference to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` MEANS
    IF `the shares are redeemed or purchased wholly or partly out of the proceeds of a fresh issue`
       AND `the aggregate amount of the proceeds` LESS THAN `the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased`
       AND (NOT (`the company is a private company` AND `in addition to the proceeds of the fresh issue the company applies a payment out of capital under Chapter 5 or under section 692(1ZA) in making the redemption or purchase`))
    THEN `the aggregate nominal value of the shares redeemed or purchased` MINUS `the aggregate amount of the proceeds`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If— (a) ..., and (b) ..., the amount of the difference must be transferred"; "This does not apply in the case of a private company if, in addition to the proceeds of the fresh issue, the company applies a payment out of capital"

-- src:9629 | (4) The amount by which a company's share capital is diminished in accordance with section 729(4) (on the cancellation of shares held as treasury shares) must be transferred to the capital redemption reserve.
@ref s 733(4) The amount by which the share capital is diminished on the cancellation of treasury shares must be transferred to the capital redemption reserve (src:9629-9629)
GIVEN `shares held as treasury shares are cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount by which the share capital is diminished in accordance with section 729(4)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 733(4) the amount to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` MEANS
    IF `shares held as treasury shares are cancelled`
    THEN `the amount by which the share capital is diminished in accordance with section 729(4)`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The amount by which a company's share capital is diminished in accordance with section 729(4) (on the cancellation of shares held as treasury shares)"

-- src:9630 | (5) The company may use the capital redemption reserve to pay up new shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares.
@ref s 733(5) The company may use the capital redemption reserve to pay up new shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares (src:9630-9630)
GIVEN `the new shares are to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 733(5) the company may use the capital redemption reserve to pay up the new shares` MEANS
    IF `the new shares are to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company may use the capital redemption reserve to pay up new shares to be allotted to members as fully paid bonus shares"

-- A rule of reading: "the provisions of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital apply as if the capital
-- redemption reserve were part of its paid up share capital".
-- src:9631 | (6) Subject to that, the provisions of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital apply as if the capital redemption reserve were part of its paid up share capital.
@ref s 733(6) The provisions relating to the reduction of share capital apply as if the capital redemption reserve were part of the paid up share capital (src:9631-9631)
GIVEN `the provision is one of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's paid up share capital` IS A NUMBER
      `the capital redemption reserve` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 733(6) the paid up share capital to take for the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is one of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital`
    THEN `the company's paid up share capital` PLUS `the capital redemption reserve`
    ELSE `the company's paid up share capital` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the rule is for "the provisions of the Companies Acts relating to the reduction of a company's share capital"

-- ---- s 734: accounting consequences of payment out of capital -----------------------------------------------

-- src:9633 | (1) This section applies where a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5 (redemption or purchase of own shares by private company out of capital) or section 692(1ZA).
@ref s 734(1) This section applies where a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5 or section 692(1ZA) (src:9633-9633)
GIVEN `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with section 692(1ZA)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5` OR `a payment out of capital is made in accordance with section 692(1ZA)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a payment out of capital is made in accordance with Chapter 5 (...) or section 692(1ZA)"

-- src:9634 | (1A) In relation to a payment under section 692(1ZA) references to the permissible capital payment are to the purchase price of the shares or (if less) the part of it met out of the payment under section 692(1ZA) and any proceeds of a fresh issue used to make the purchase.
@ref s 734(1A) For a payment under section 692(1ZA) the permissible capital payment is the purchase price or, if less, the part of it met out of that payment and any proceeds of a fresh issue (src:9634-9634)
GIVEN `the purchase price of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the payment under section 692(1ZA)` IS A NUMBER
      `the proceeds of a fresh issue used to make the purchase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734(1A) the permissible capital payment for a payment under section 692(1ZA)` MEANS
    IF `the purchase price of the shares` AT MOST (`the payment under section 692(1ZA)` PLUS `the proceeds of a fresh issue used to make the purchase`)
    THEN `the purchase price of the shares`
    ELSE `the payment under section 692(1ZA)` PLUS `the proceeds of a fresh issue used to make the purchase`

-- src:9640 | (4) Where the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied by the company in making a redemption or purchase of its own shares in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5, the references in subsections (2) and (3) to the permissible capital payment are to be read as referring to the aggregate of that payment and those proceeds.
@ref s 734(4) Where the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5, the references to the permissible capital payment are to the aggregate of that payment and those proceeds (src:9640-9640)
GIVEN `the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permissible capital payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the proceeds of the fresh issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734(4) the amount to read as the permissible capital payment in subsections (2) and (3)` MEANS
    IF `the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5`
    THEN `the permissible capital payment` PLUS `the proceeds of the fresh issue`
    ELSE `the permissible capital payment` -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the proceeds of a fresh issue are applied by the company in making a redemption or purchase of its own shares in addition to a payment out of capital under Chapter 5"

-- src:9635 | (2) If the permissible capital payment is less than the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased, the amount of the difference must be transferred to the company's capital redemption reserve.
@ref s 734(2) If the permissible capital payment is less than the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased, the difference must be transferred to the capital redemption reserve (src:9635-9635)
GIVEN `the permissible capital payment, as subsections (1A) and (4) read it` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734(2) the amount to be transferred to the capital redemption reserve` MEANS
    IF `the permissible capital payment, as subsections (1A) and (4) read it` LESS THAN `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased`
    THEN `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased` MINUS `the permissible capital payment, as subsections (1A) and (4) read it`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the permissible capital payment is less than the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased"

DECLARE `s 734(3) what may be reduced` IS ONE OF
    `s 734(3)(a) the amount of any capital redemption reserve`
    `s 734(3)(a) the amount of any share premium account`
    `s 734(3)(a) the amount of any fully paid share capital of the company`
    `s 734(3)(b) any amount representing unrealised profits standing to the credit of a revaluation reserve maintained by the company`
    `s 734(3) any other amount`

-- src:9636 | (3) If the permissible capital payment is greater than the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased—
-- src:9637 | (a) the amount of any capital redemption reserve, share premium account or fully paid share capital of the company, and
-- src:9638 | (b) any amount representing unrealised profits of the company for the time being standing to the credit of any revaluation reserve maintained by the company,
-- src:9639 | may be reduced by a sum not exceeding (or by sums not in total exceeding) the amount by which the permissible capital payment exceeds the nominal amount of the shares.
@ref s 734(3) If the permissible capital payment is greater than the nominal amount, the reserves may be reduced by a sum not exceeding the excess (src:9636-9639)
GIVEN `the permissible capital payment, as subsections (1A) and (4) read it` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 734(3) the most by which the amounts may be reduced` MEANS
    IF `the permissible capital payment, as subsections (1A) and (4) read it` GREATER THAN `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased`
    THEN `the permissible capital payment, as subsections (1A) and (4) read it` MINUS `the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased`
    ELSE 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the permissible capital payment is greater than the nominal amount of the shares redeemed or purchased"

@ref s 734(3) The capital redemption reserve, share premium account, fully paid share capital and unrealised profits in a revaluation reserve may be reduced (src:9636-9639)
GIVEN item IS A `s 734(3) what may be reduced`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 734(3) the amount may be reduced` MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `s 734(3) any other amount` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names four amounts and does not close the list with "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 735: effect of company's failure to redeem or purchase -------------------------------------------------

-- src:9642 | (1) This section applies where a company—
-- src:9643 | (a) issues shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed, or
-- src:9644 | (b) agrees to purchase any of its shares.
@ref s 735(1) This section applies where a company issues shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed, or agrees to purchase any of its shares (src:9642-9644)
GIVEN `the company issues shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company agrees to purchase any of its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company issues shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed` OR `the company agrees to purchase any of its shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a company— (a) issues shares on terms that they are or are liable to be redeemed, or (b) agrees to purchase any of its shares"

-- src:9645 | (2) The company is not liable in damages in respect of any failure on its part to redeem or purchase any of the shares.
@ref s 735(2) The company is not liable in damages in respect of any failure on its part to redeem or purchase any of the shares (src:9645-9645)
GIVEN `s 735(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company has failed to redeem or purchase the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(2) the company is liable in damages for the failure` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 735(1) this section applies`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `the company has failed to redeem or purchase the shares`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company is not liable in damages in respect of any failure on its part to redeem or purchase any of the shares."
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any failure on its part to redeem or purchase"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the section applies is not known

DECLARE `s 735(2) right of the holder` IS ONE OF
    `s 735(2) a right to sue the company for damages in respect of its failure to redeem or purchase`
    `s 735(2) any other right of the holder of the shares`

-- src:9646 | This is without prejudice to any right of the holder of the shares other than his right to sue the company for damages in respect of its failure.
@ref s 735(2) This is without prejudice to any right of the holder other than his right to sue the company for damages (src:9646-9646)
GIVEN right IS A `s 735(2) right of the holder`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(2) the holder's right survives the failure` MEANS
    CONSIDER right
    WHEN `s 735(2) a right to sue the company for damages in respect of its failure to redeem or purchase` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than his right to sue the company for damages in respect of its failure"
    WHEN `s 735(2) any other right of the holder of the shares` THEN JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 735(3) act of the court` IS ONE OF
    `s 735(3) grant an order for specific performance of the terms of redemption or purchase`

-- src:9647 | (3) The court shall not grant an order for specific performance of the terms of redemption or purchase if the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits.
@ref s 735(3) The court shall not grant an order for specific performance if the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs out of distributable profits (src:9647-9647)
GIVEN `the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(3) the court shall not grant specific performance` MEANS
    IF `the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits"

@ref s 735(3) The court shall not grant an order for specific performance if the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs out of distributable profits (src:9647-9647)
GIVEN `the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 735(3) act of the court`
`s 735(3) the court shant grant an order for specific performance` MEANS
    IF `the company shows that it is unable to meet the costs of redeeming or purchasing the shares in question out of distributable profits`
    THEN PARTY Court
         SHANT `s 735(3) grant an order for specific performance of the terms of redemption or purchase`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Court BECAUSE "s 735(3): the court granted an order for specific performance although the company showed that it is unable to meet the costs out of distributable profits"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:9648 | (4) If the company is wound up and at the commencement of the winding up any of the shares have not been redeemed or purchased, the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company.
-- src:9649 | When shares are redeemed or purchased under this subsection, they are treated as cancelled.
@ref s 735(4) If the company is wound up and shares have not been redeemed or purchased, the terms may be enforced against the company, and the shares are treated as cancelled (src:9648-9649)
GIVEN `the company is wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the commencement of the winding up any of the shares have not been redeemed or purchased` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 735(5) subsection (4) does not apply` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(4) the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company` MEANS
    -- fork F-grant-735-4: "the terms of redemption or purchase may be enforced against the company" ("If the company is wound up ...") is a grant or a power; where its gate fails the answer is NOTHING; the other reading answers JUST FALSE (a failed "if" read as the text's own no); the branch where subsection (5) takes the case out of subsection (4) keeps JUST FALSE, which is the text's own "does not apply"
    IF (NOT `the company is wound up`) OR (NOT `at the commencement of the winding up any of the shares have not been redeemed or purchased`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the company is wound up and at the commencement of the winding up any of the shares have not been redeemed or purchased": the terms' enforceability outside a winding up is not what the subsection says
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 735(5) subsection (4) does not apply`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply if"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (5) takes the case out of subsection (4) is not known

@ref s 735(4) When shares are redeemed or purchased under this subsection, they are treated as cancelled (src:9649-9649)
GIVEN `the shares are redeemed or purchased under section 735(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(4) the shares are treated as cancelled` MEANS
    IF `the shares are redeemed or purchased under section 735(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When shares are redeemed or purchased under this subsection, they are treated as cancelled"

-- src:9650 | (5) Subsection (4) does not apply if—
-- src:9651 | (a) the terms provided for the redemption or purchase to take place at a date later than that of the commencement of the winding up, or
-- src:9652 | (b) during the period—
-- src:9653 | (i) beginning with the date on which the redemption or purchase was to have taken place, and
-- src:9654 | (ii) ending with the commencement of the winding up,
-- src:9655 | the company could not at any time have lawfully made a distribution equal in value to the price at which the shares were to have been redeemed or purchased.
@ref s 735(5) Subsection (4) does not apply if the terms provided for a later date or the company could not have lawfully made a distribution equal to the price between the date it was due and the winding up (src:9650-9655)
GIVEN `the date on which the redemption or purchase was to take place under the terms` IS A DATE
      `the date of the commencement of the winding up` IS A DATE
      `during the period from the date on which the redemption or purchase was to have taken place to the commencement of the winding up the company could not at any time have lawfully made a distribution equal in value to the price` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(5) subsection (4) does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the redemption or purchase was to take place under the terms` GREATER THAN `the date of the commencement of the winding up`
       OR `during the period from the date on which the redemption or purchase was to have taken place to the commencement of the winding up the company could not at any time have lawfully made a distribution equal in value to the price`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply if— (a) the terms provided for the redemption or purchase to take place at a date later than that of the commencement of the winding up, or (b) during the period ... the company could not at any time have lawfully made a distribution equal in value to the price"

-- src:9656 | (6) There shall be paid in priority to any amount that the company is liable under subsection (4) to pay in respect of any shares—
-- src:9657 | (a) all other debts and liabilities of the company (other than any due to members in their character as such), and
-- src:9658 | (b) if other shares carry rights (whether as to capital or as to income) that are preferred to the rights as to capital attaching to the first-mentioned shares, any amount due in satisfaction of those preferred rights.
-- src:9659 | Subject to that, any such amount shall be paid in priority to any amounts due to members in satisfaction of their rights (whether as to capital or income) as members.
@ref s 735(6) Amounts paid in priority to any amount payable under subsection (4) (src:9656-9659)
GIVEN claim IS A `s 735(6) other claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 735(6) the claim is paid in priority to any amount the company is liable under subsection (4) to pay` MEANS
    CONSIDER claim
    WHEN `s 735(6)(a) a debt or liability of the company other than one due to members in their character as such` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 735(6)(b) an amount due in satisfaction of rights as to capital or income preferred to the rights as to capital attaching to the shares` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 735(6) an amount due to members in satisfaction of their rights as members, other than preferred rights` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to that, any such amount shall be paid in priority to any amounts due to members in satisfaction of their rights (whether as to capital or income) as members": the amount under subsection (4) ranks ahead of them, so they do not rank ahead of it
    WHEN `s 735(6) a claim of another kind` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (6) ranks the three kinds of claim it names and no other

-- ---- s 736: meaning of "distributable profits" ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9661 | In this Part (except in Chapter 2 (financial assistance): see section 683) “distributable profits”, in relation to the making of any payment by a company, means profits out of which the company could lawfully make a distribution (within the meaning given by section 830) equal in value to the payment.
@ref s 736 "Distributable profits" in this Part, in relation to the making of any payment, means profits out of which the company could lawfully make a distribution equal in value to the payment (src:9661-9661)
GIVEN `the provision is in Chapter 2 of Part 18 (financial assistance)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 830 the profits available for distribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 736 the profits are distributable profits in relation to the payment` MEANS
    IF `the provision is in Chapter 2 of Part 18 (financial assistance)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this Part (except in Chapter 2 (financial assistance): see section 683)": section 683 gives the meaning there
    ELSE IF `s 830 the profits available for distribution` AT LEAST `the value of the payment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“distributable profits”, in relation to the making of any payment by a company, means profits out of which the company could lawfully make a distribution (within the meaning given by section 830) equal in value to the payment"
